  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\nThis approach employs a multi-resolution optimization with a constrained evolutionary strategy to minimize the overlap integral. The core idea is to enforce the minimum cut representation for the step function elements using binary where h[i] is close to 0.5 or must have derivative-like behavior at transitions. This prevents the axis-aligned DE method from getting stuck in local minima. The algorithm uses explicit step boundary enforcement with tight constraint handling, and incorporates phase transitions from low to high resolution with dimensionality increase to be systematic.\n\nBottlenecks addressed:\n- Previous methods had poor step control (forced continuous values when binary representation was optimal)\n- Used rigid gradient-free methods unsuited for non-convex spaces with complex constraints\n- Failed to systematically resolve the trade-off between step height and width optimization\n\nSignificant improvements over inspiration:\n1.  - Binary mutation instead of continuous mutation\n2.  - Active constraint enforcement at boundaries (avoiding off-assignments)\n3.  -\u5366\u578b\u641c\u7d22\u53d6\u4ee3\u524d\u4ee3\u7684\u968f\u673a\u6270\u52a8\n4.  - Parametric score modification instead of logarithmic approximations\n\n2. Mathematical specification:\n\nObjective:\nMinimize: C5 = (1/n) * max_k [ \u2211_{i=0}^{n-1} h[i] * (1 - h[(i+k) % n]) ]\n\nBut now for competitive results, compute by:\n    C5 = (2.0 / n) * max_k( corr[k] )  [using mode='full' correlation]\nwhere corr[k] = \u2211_{i=0}^{2n-2} h_vec[i] * (1 - h_vec[(i+k)]) for i+k within bounds, with cyclic continuation outside bounds (to approximate circular correlation on [0,2])\n\nVariables:\n- h_vec: vector of n elements [0,1]\n- k: integer lag from -(n-1) to n-1\n\nBinary Constraint Formulation:\nmap any candidate h_vec to a binary representation:\n\n   Let \u03b4 = 0.01  # Tolerance\n   On recipe change between i and i+1:\n\n   Define binary state s_i = 1 if h_vec[i] >= 0.9 or h_vec[i] <= 0.1 else 1 if h_vec[i+1]-h_vec[i] > 0 else s_i-1\n\n   Then ensure transitions:\n        if s_i changes between i-1 and i, then force h_vec[i] to be around 0.5\n        if s_i-1, s_i = s_i+1, then force h_vec[i] to not be too close to 0 or 1\n\nConstraints through mutation template:\n\n   h_new = f(parent, p=0.2)  # 80% chance to remain, 20% for small changes\n\n   For constraints:\n        If random < 0.1, force one element to 0.5\n        If random < 0.1, increment/decrement a step\n\n   Sum constraint through post-processing projection if necessary.\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n\nPhase 1: Dimension building and constraint initialization:\n\n   n0 = n_initial\n   base_h = initial_h_values  # Provided parent solution\n\n   def project_feasible(h_vec, target_sum):\n        s = np.sum(h_vec)\n        ratio = target_sum / s\n        if abs(ratio-1.0) < 1e-8: return h_vec.clip(0,1)\n        # Scale equally or Adaptive: try to balance spans\n        h_scaled = h_vec * ratio\n        loc = np.diff(np.sort(h_vec)).argmax()  \n        # Preserve one point from around 0.5 if present\n        if np.abs(h_scaled[loc]-0.5) < 0.1:\n        h_scaled[loc] = 0.5 * (1.0 - np.random.random())\n        return h_scaled.clip(0,1)\n\n   h_current = project_feasible(base_h, n0/2.0)\n\nPhase 2: Core Evolution (Binary-Aware Evolution Strategy):\n    def smooth_obj_for_DE(x, alpha=0.01):\n        # x shape (n,)\n        h_vec = x\n        corr = np.correlate(h_vec, 1.0-h_vec, mode='full')\n        best_score = np.max(corr) * (2.0/n0)  # Scale to original domain\n        return alpha * (best_score - alpha) **(10) + alpha\n\n    # Constrain mutation to binary changes with tolerance\n    bounds = [(0,1)] * n0\n\n    # DE variant with binary mutation template:\n    def differential_evolution_round(prev, seed, max_iter=100, fevals=300):\n        pop_size = 30\n        new_search = []\n        for i in range(pop_size):\n            candidate = prev * (0.95 + np.random.randn(len(prev)) * 0.05)\n            # Contraint handling: enforce binary structure\n            diff_idx = list(3-find these continuous regions)\n\n        # This function stub requires substantial implementation of full DE algorithm with binary constraints\n\n    return h_opt, score\n\nPhase 3: Resolution Ratcheting:\n\n    n_layers = [50, 100, 200, 400, 800]\n    n_base = 50\n    h_base = ...  # Output from previous successful resolution\n\n    def interpolate_upscale():\n        # Use Linear/Log interpolation between layers\n\n    def multi_pop_evolve():\n        # Constrain to binary-like patterned mutation\n\n    final_resolution = 800\n\nPhase 4: Hybrid Subgradient Polish:\n\n    mid_point = sum(h_vec)/len(h_vec) * 2.0 - 1.0  # Space transform\n\n    def lag_sensitive_gradient(h):\n        corr = np.correlate(h, 1.0-h, mode='none')  # Only leading terms?\n        mid = len(h)//2\n        lags_of_interest = sorted(np.argpartition(corr, -5)[-5:])[-5:]\n        grad = np.zeros_like(h)\n        for lag in lags_of_interest:\n            if lag > 10: break  # Compute avoid overflow\n            indices = mid + np.arange(-lag, lag)\n            h0 = h[mid - lag]\n            h1 = h[mid + lag]\n            # Compute directional gradient\n            ... \n        return grad\n\n    # Use projected gradient with 10 iterations (free parameters adaptive)\n\n    Initial learning_rate = 0x.5\n    for iter in range(10):\n        grad = lag_sensitive_gradient(h_base)\n        # Add strong constraint at boundaries (impulse)\n        # Project to keep binary-like structure\n\n        candidate = h_base - step_size * grad\n        candidate = project_feasible(candidate, target)\n\nPhase 5: Boundary Impulse Enforcement (Binary or Deallocation):\n    def enforce_binary_pattern(human, steps=3):\n        # Formulate decision boundaries from lag data\n\n    # Called if solution won't tighten with main strategy\n\n4. Search Choices:\n\n   - Initial population: Use initial_h_values as anchor\n   - DE params:\n        strategy = 'strife'\n        dynamic_weight = 0.2  # Force anti-parallel momentum\n        static mutation = 0.2\n\n5. Compute Budget:\n\n   Time allocation:\n      Initial DE runs @ 50 points: 300 seconds\n      Upper resolution layer expansion: 400 seconds (n=50 to n=800)\n      Final polish with constrained IP: 600 seconds\n\n   Total within 1300 seconds.\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\n\n   - C5 = float(np.correlate(h_final, 1.0-h_final, mode='full').max()) * (2.0 / n_final)\n   - Project final solution to meet:\n          0 <= h[i] <= 1 for all i\n          absolute_sum(h) \u2261 n_final/2 within 1e-8\n   - Returns (h_values, C5, n_points)",
